# Snatch It — web environment contract
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. In production these are set in the
# Vercel project (Settings -> Environment Variables), NOT in a file.
#
# Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_ except SENTRY_DSN, i.e. it is compiled into
# the client bundle and is publicly visible. That is correct for all of them —
# they are public-class credentials. The Supabase SERVICE ROLE key must never
# appear in this app under any name: every privileged operation lives in a
# Supabase edge function. If you find yourself wanting it here, the operation
# belongs in an edge function instead.

# ── Required. The app REFUSES TO START in production without these ──────────
# Missing Supabase env used to degrade silently to fixture listings served
# with HTTP 200 — a misconfigured deploy looked like a working marketplace
# selling tickets that do not exist. src/lib/env.ts now throws instead.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Required for checkout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Publishable key only (pk_test_… / pk_live_…). Must match the mode of the
# secret key configured on the Supabase edge functions, or PaymentIntents will
# be created in one mode and confirmed in the other.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Canonical origin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for metadataBase, canonicals, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, and the Stripe
# checkout return_url. Wrong value = broken post-payment redirect.
# No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://snatchti.com

# ── Optional: error reporting ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a DSN, captureException() still console.errors, so failures land in
# the platform log — they just do not reach Sentry. Set this in production.
# Either name works; NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required for client-side boundaries
# (app/error.tsx, app/global-error.tsx) to report at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ── Supplied automatically by Vercel — do not set manually ──────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_ENV               production | preview | development
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA    tags Sentry events with the release
